      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T14:37:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this would be a particularly safe use of flagging though - if the flag is disabled then the logic should be equivalent to before this change - and I think the current structure achieves that unambiguously.\n\nArguably there could be another level of method nesting added, making `SniffMidi()` just:\n\n```\nreturn flag ? SniffMidiEfficiently() : SniffMidiLegacy();\n```\n\nThen when the flag is removed `SniffMidiEfficiently()` can be in-lined into `SniffMidi()` and `SniffMidiLegacy()` can be removed.",
      "parentUuid": "27a653e0_177ccdbf",
      "range": {
